Short answer: yes — whenever possible use the exact legal name that the Social Security Administration (SSA) has on file. That prevents delays or mismatches when the organization verifies your SSN.

Details and practical steps:
- Best practice: enter your full legal name exactly as it appears on your Social Security card / SSA record (including punctuation, suffixes like Jr./III, and middle name vs. middle initial if that’s what SSA has).
- Why it matters: name/SSN mismatches can cause processing delays, rejected forms, payroll or tax-reporting errors (W‑2/1099), and problems with background checks or benefits.
