  3. If you can’t update before submitting the form, contact the organization receiving the form and ask whether they accept supporting documents (e.g., copy of SSA card, marriage certificate) or an “aka”/alias field.
  4. Keep copies of any documentation you send.
- Security reminder: avoid sharing your full SSN in unsecured messages or email. Only provide SSN information through secure portals or directly to trusted recipients and consider giving only the last four when acceptable.

