Assistant: Short answer: yes — the name on the form should match your legal name as it appears on your Social Security record (your Social Security card). Exact matches matter for many government, tax, and payroll processes; small differences can cause verification failures or delays.

Details and practical steps
- Where an exact match matters most:
  - SSA/IRS reporting (W-2s, tax withholding) and E-Verify/payroll — these systems compare name + SSN.
  - Government IDs, background checks, immigration, and some benefits enrollment.
- Minor differences that are usually tolerated:
