What to do next
- If you think the name on your form differs from your SSA record, check your SSA record first. If you need to change your SSA name (e.g., after marriage), update it with SSA before submitting forms that rely on the SSN. See ssa.gov for details and required documents.
- If you can’t update SSA immediately, ask the organization receiving the form whether they will accept the variation and what documentation they need. Some organizations can accept supporting ID temporarily; others require exact matches.
- If the mismatch is a typo on the form, ask them to correct it and re-submit.

Protecting your SSN
- Only provide the full SSN through secure, trusted channels. Prefer giving only the last four digits when the form allows it. Don’t email full SSNs over unencrypted email.

