Short answer: yes — for anything tied to your Social Security Number (payroll, taxes, benefits, government verification) the name on the form should match the name on your Social Security Administration (SSA) record. Mismatches can cause delays, rejected forms, or problems with W‑2s, E‑Verify, benefits, or background checks.

Important notes and next steps

- Don’t share your full SSN in email or chat. I won’t repeat the number you posted. If you need help, give only the last four digits when absolutely necessary and only over secure channels.
